; `(A B)` checked in signatures while no literal, no pattern and no
; runtime representation existed behind it. Products are `struct`,
; sums are `data`, so the keyword-headed group is refused with
; migration advice rather than parsed into a shape no value inhabits.
;
; `.axbad` because the refusal is at parse time. `()` is untouched:
; it is unit, and widely used.
(:: takes (-> (Int Bool) Int))
